    dm:pageAccuracyNote "The notes add that a trust that keeps marketing lots risks unrelated business income and the 100 percent excise tax." ;
    dm:authorityOutcome dm:NeedsCounsel ;
    dm:authorityBasis "26 USC 512(b)(5), read 2026-11-21: gains from selling property are excluded except for inventory and property held primarily for sale to customers in a trade or business. A trust that keeps selling a subdivider's lots earns business income, taxed in full under 664(c)(2)(A), read." ;
    dm:authorityRead true .
:S4_56_gift a dm:PlannedGift ;
    dm:giftVehicle dm:CharitableRemainderUnitrust ; dm:deductionAllowed true ; dm:deductionFor dm:RemainderInterest ;
    dm:unitrustPercent "5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    # assumed: remainder share worked out from the page's deduction and funding figures
    dm:remainderValuePercent "35"^^xsd:decimal ;
    # regraded on primary law: the trust keeps selling the subdivider's lots, which are property
    # held for sale to customers, so the gain is not excluded (512(b)(5))
    dm:producesUBTI true .

