:S4_97 a dm:StoryCase ;
    dm:storyId "S4-97" ;
    dm:storySection "4.8.1" ;
    dm:storyKind "case" ;
    dm:pageSays "A unitrust with unrelated business income from an operating partnership; the page cites the case for the 100 percent excise tax." ;
    dm:citesAuthority "Newhall Unitrust (1995/1997); 664(c)(2)(A)" ;
    dm:pageOutcome dm:NeedsCounsel ;
    dm:storyScope dm:GradedByModel ;
    dm:storyGift :S4_97_gift ;
    dm:pageAccuracyNote "The notes say the case applied the pre-2007 rule that cost the trust its exemption, so it does not support the excise tax enacted in 2006." ;
    dm:citedForOpposite "Newhall Unitrust (9th Cir. 1997), read 2026-11-21 on the appeals opinion (the Tax Court opinion, 104 T.C. 236, not read): under 664(c) as it then stood, any unrelated business taxable income cost the trust its exemption for the year. It predates the 100 percent excise tax and does not support it." ;
    dm:citedAuthorityRead true ;
    dm:authorityOutcome dm:NeedsCounsel ;
    dm:authorityBasis "26 USC 664(c)(2)(A), read 2026-11-21: the excise tax equal to the unrelated business taxable income, for tax years after 2006. The page's outcome stands on the statute, not on the case." ;
    dm:authorityRead true .
:S4_97_gift a dm:PlannedGift ;
    dm:giftVehicle dm:CharitableRemainderUnitrust ; dm:deductionAllowed true ; dm:deductionFor dm:RemainderInterest ;
